{
  "_comment": [
    "M7.1 fixture: the wireless uplink.",
    "",
    "One physical radio in CLIENT mode, associated and carrying the default",
    "route, plus one unused Ethernet port.",
    "",
    "The point of this fixture is the asymmetry: a wireless client is a",
    "perfectly reasonable uplink and a poor LAN, and an analysis that treated",
    "radio and wired NIC as interchangeable would get one of those two wrong.",
    "",
    "The radio 'wlp9s2' carries a `wireless` object with no mode in it, which",
        "is what a host looks like when the mode could not be read. That is the",
        "case the rule against inferring access-point capability is tested against:",
        "with the mode unobserved, THN must say so rather than assume either way."
  ],
